// Copilot key (ASUS ROG): the firmware sends Shift+Super+F23.
//
// Stock xkeyboard-config defines <FK23> with type "PC_SHIFT_SUPER_LEVEL2" and
// produces XF86Assistant on level 2. That caused two problems:
//   1) Qt 6 does not know XF86Assistant, so the KDE shortcut dialog only shows
//      "Meta+Shift" and the key cannot be bound.
//   2) That type "consumes" Shift+Super to select level 2. The capture dialog
//      saw the raw modifiers and stored Meta+Shift+F19, but KWin drops consumed
//      modifiers when matching, so the shortcut never fired.
//
// Fix: make the key ONE_LEVEL so it always produces plain F19. No modifiers
// are consumed and there is no level ambiguity; Shift+Super reach KWin as real
// modifiers and the shortcut matches as Meta+Shift+F19.
// The plain F23 meaning of this key is not used on this machine.
partial function_keys
xkb_symbols "f19" {
    key <FK23> {
        type[Group1] = "ONE_LEVEL",
        symbols[Group1] = [ F19 ]
    };
};
